rix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile env/global-state variant executed when tests or code read process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a fix SHA or explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per security surface. Write `N/A` with a reason when none applies. GOOD: CHK-030 [P0] The script reads no credential. WEAK: Security is fine. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation implemented\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] Auth/authz working correctly\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per document that must agree. GOOD: CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md` and `tasks.md` name the same flag. WEAK: Docs are updated. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Code comments adequate\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file location rule. GOOD: CHK-050 [P1] Test copies live under `scratch/test/`. WEAK: Files are organized. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files in scratch/ only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] scratch/ cleaned before completion\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n<!-- FILL: Count the boxes by priority and write the three totals. GOOD: P0 12, P1 13, P2 1. WEAK: Most items done. -->\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | [X] | [ ]/[X] |\n| P1 Items | [Y] | [ ]/[Y] |\n| P2 Items | [Z] | [ ]/[Z] |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per ADR, or delete the section when the packet records no ADR. GOOD: CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed by T002. WEAK: Architecture is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] Architecture decisions documented in decision-record.md\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] All ADRs have status (Proposed/Accepted)\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path documented (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per performance claim, or delete the section when the packet makes none. GOOD: CHK-110 [P1] The flag adds under 5 ms. WEAK: Performance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] Response time targets met (NFR-P01)\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Throughput targets met (NFR-P02)\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing completed\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Performance benchmarks documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per deployment step, or delete the section when the packet ships no service. GOOD: CHK-120 [P0] The rollback command was run in a copy. WEAK: Ready to deploy. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and tested\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] Feature flag configured (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] Monitoring/alerting configured\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook created\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment runbook reviewed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per compliance surface, or delete the section when none applies. GOOD: CHK-130 [P1] No license changed. WEAK: Compliance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review completed\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses compatible\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10 checklist completed\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling compliant with requirements\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per document pair that must agree, or delete the section when the packet holds no paired documents. GOOD: CHK-140 [P1] `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the three phases. WEAK: Docs are verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Name the real approver for each role. Delete a row when the role does not exist. Write `N/A` or delete the section when no sign-off applies. GOOD: Conductor, runs every task. Operator, merges the commit. WEAK: Signed off. -->\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>. No task is ticked: this packet plans the change and does not build it.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed, with the evidence named on the line |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nEvery task below is open. This packet is a planning artifact: it describes the change and the proof, and the banned-operation list forbids editing the script from here. A ticked box would claim an implementation that does not exist. The baselines the tasks refer to were measured on 2026-10-25 and are restated in the task text so the implementer can compare rather than re-derive.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the output block at `recommend-level.sh:502-558` and record the line counts for the three shapes. Verify: `wc -l` prints `17` for the full default run, `12` with `--no-recommend-phases` and `36` with `--json` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T002 Capture those three outputs into `scratch/baseline/` so the verification phase can diff rather than eyeball. Verify: `ls scratch/baseline` lists `default.txt`, `no-phases.txt` and `json.txt` (`scratch/baseline/`)\n- [ ] T003 [P] Record the two suite baselines on the unmodified script. Verify: `node tests/test-phase-validation.js` prints `passed=51 failed=0` and `node tests/test-phase-system.js` prints `passed=27 failed=0` (`runtime/cli/tests/`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add `output_level_line()` to section 4 and replace the inline echo at line 510 with a call to it. Verify: the default output diffs clean against `scratch/baseline/default.txt` (`recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T005 Add `QUIET=false` to section 2's globals and a `--quiet|-q)` branch to section 5's `case`. Verify: `bash -n` exits 0 and `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` shows both the global and the branch (`recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T006 Add `output_quiet()` that calls `output_level_line()` and returns. Verify: `--quiet --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural` prints exactly 1 line (`recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T007 Add the conflict guard after the parse loop, ahead of the dispatch: `--quiet` with `--json` exits 1 and writes both flag names to stderr. Verify: the run's stdout is empty and its exit status is 1 (`recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T008 Order the dispatch as conflict guard, quiet, JSON, text. Verify: all three existing shapes diff clean against their baselines (`recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T009 Add `--quiet, -q` to the header OPTIONS block and to `show_help()`. Verify: `rg -c 'quiet, -q' recommend-level.sh` prints `2` and `--help` lists the flag (`recommend-level.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Replay the thirteen-row matrix and record the result of each row. Verify: every row matches the expectation in the list below (`scratch/evidence/matrix.txt`)\n- [ ] T011 Compare the quiet line against the text report's line 2 byte for byte. Verify: `diff` exits 0 between the quiet output and `sed -n '2p'` of the default run (`scratch/evidence/quiet-vs-line2.diff`)\n- [ ] T012 Run the exact command each YAML asset runs, with `--json --recommend-phases --phase-threshold 25 --loc 500 --files 8`, and parse the output. Verify: `node -e 'JSON.parse(...)'` exits 0 and the object still has its 36 lines (`scratch/evidence/yaml-callers.txt`)\n- [ ] T013 Rerun both Node suites on the changed script. Verify: `passed=51 failed=0` and `passed=27 failed=0`, unchanged from T003 (`scratch/evidence/suites.txt`)\n- [ ] T014 Run `validate.sh --strict` on this packet. Verify: the last line reads `RESULT: PASSED` (`specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag`)\n\n### T010 matrix rows\n\n| Row | Invocation | Expected |\n|-----|------------|----------|\n| 1 | `--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural` | 17 lines, exit 0 |\n| 2 | row 1 plus `--no-recommend-phases` | 12 lines, exit 0 |\n| 3 | row 1 plus `--json` | 36 lines, exit 0, parses as JSON |\n| 4 | row 1 plus `--quiet` | 1 line, exit 0 |\n| 5 | row 1 plus `-q` | 1 line, byte-identical to row 4 |\n| 6 | row 1 plus `--quiet --json` | exit 1, empty stdout, stderr names both |\n| 7 | row 1 plus `--json --quiet` | identical to row 6, proving order independence |\n| 8 | `--quiet` with no `--loc` or `--files` | exit 1, empty stdout, usage error on stderr |\n| 9 | row 1 plus `--quiet=1` | exit 1, unknown option, empty stdout |\n| 10 | row 1 plus `-qj` | exit 1, unknown option; the parser does not bundle short flags |\n| 11 | `--loc --quiet` | exit 1, `--loc requires a numeric value` |\n| 12 | row 1 plus `--quiet --quiet` | 1 line, identical to row 4 |\n| 13 | `--help --quiet` | help text, exit 0; help short-circuits every mode |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] The three existing shapes diff clean against `scratch/baseline/` and both suites hold 51 and 27 passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\nA blocked row stays `[ ]` with a `[B]` marker and the reason on the line. A row that reads N/A is closed by the reason it states, not by a tick.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [x] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in `spec.md`: REQ-001 to REQ-007, each naming a command or an observable output\n- [x] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in `plan.md`: one shared emitter, one new mode, one conflict guard\n- [x] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available: bash 3.2, `wc`, `diff`, `sed` and Node, all present in this checkout\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No new shellcheck-class warning: the new branch uses the same `case` and `[[ ]]` forms as its neighbours\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] The conflict guard writes to stderr and leaves stdout empty\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The new function follows the file's existing section-4 shape: a comment, then `output_*`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met: every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` reads Met\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The thirteen matrix rows in T010 each match their expectation\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested: no-input, repeated flag, `--quiet=1`, `-qj` and `--loc --quiet`\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated: exit 1 and empty stdout on every rejected combination\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\nThis packet adds a feature rather than closing a finding, so the finding-class and fix-SHA rows do not apply. The inventory rows still do, because the change alters a surface other files consume.\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed: `rg -n 'Recommended Level' .skilled/` returns one code producer at `recommend-level.sh:510`; every other hit is a template hint or a golden snapshot of one\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Consumer inventory completed: the two YAML call sites, the two Node suites and the prose references are listed in `plan.md` section 3\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P1] Matrix axes and row count listed before implementation: T010 carries thirteen rows across quiet, JSON, help and input validity\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] Argument-parser adversarial rows present: `--quiet=1`, `-qj`, `--loc --quiet`, a repeated flag and reversed flag order\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets: the script holds none and the change adds none\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation preserved: `--quiet` does not bypass the numeric checks or the empty-input check\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] N/A: the script has no authentication or authorization surface to test\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md` and `tasks.md` name the same flag, the same three line counts and the same conflict rule\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Both help surfaces list the flag: the header OPTIONS block and `show_help()`\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] `README.md` needs no change: it names no flags. Its broken example at line 514 is out of scope, as `spec.md` section 3 records\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Baselines and probe output live under `scratch/` only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` holds only the baseline and evidence files at completion, with no stray copy of the script\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 13 | 2/13 |\n| P1 Items | 22 | 1/22 |\n| P2 Items | 9 | 0/9 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n\nThe three verified rows are the pre-implementation checks, which the packet itself satisfies. Every implementation and verification row is open, because no code changed.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed: the level literal is emitted by one function that both output paths call\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] Both ADRs carry a status: ADR-001 and ADR-002 each read Proposed\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale: each ADR names at least two rejected options and why\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] N/A: no migration path. The change adds a mode and removes nothing\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] NFR-P01 holds: the quiet path returns before the breakdown and phase echoes, so it cannot be slower than the default path\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] N/A: the script makes no throughput claim\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] N/A: no load to test; the script is invoked once per call\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] N/A: no benchmark to document; the comparison in CHK-110 is structural\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback documented and exercised: revert the commit and rerun the three shapes and both suites\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] N/A: no feature flag. The CLI flag is the surface, and removing the branch removes the feature\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] N/A: no monitoring. The script runs in a repository rather than a service\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] N/A: no runbook. `--help` is the operating document\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] N/A: nothing to review beyond CHK-120\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] N/A: no security surface changes, so no review is required beyond CHK-030 and CHK-031\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] No dependency license change: the change adds no dependency\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] N/A: no web surface, so no OWASP checklist applies\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] N/A: the script handles no personal or regulated data\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the flag name, the three counts and the conflict rule\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] N/A: no API documentation. The help text is the interface, and CHK-041 covers it\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] No user-facing document lists the script's flags, so none needs updating\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] N/A: single-session packet, no knowledge transfer\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| Operator (dispatch) | Technical Lead | [ ] Pending | |\n| Operator | Product Owner | [ ] Pending | |\n| Reviewer | QA Lead | [ ] Pending | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n---\n\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n- [ ] Read the task's target region in `recommend-level.sh` before editing it, and confirm the line numbers still match the section named\n- [ ] Confirm `scratch/baseline/` holds the three captured outputs before touching the output block\n- [ ] Confirm `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0 on the unmodified file, so a later failure is attributable\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Run T001 to T009 in order. T010 onward runs only after the script parses |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Modify `recommend-level.sh` only. The two YAML assets, the two suites and the templates stay untouched |\n| TASK-PROOF | Every task names its verification command. A task with no observed output stays open |\n| TASK-BASELINE | Compare against the captured baseline rather than a remembered count. 17, 12 and 36 are the numbers to match |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\n\nAfter each task: `Task T### complete. Files modified: <list>. Verify: <command> printed <observed output>.`\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\n\nIf a task cannot be completed: stop, mark it `[B]` with the reason on the line, write the blocker and what was tried into `scratch/`, and report it. Do not widen scope to route around a blocker, and do not tick a box whose verification was not observed.\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":118,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":87}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
